## Whole-file declarations, data, registration and contextual obligations (unit-1)

Defines a300px square positioned container and a100px square named anchor offset80px left and130px top. Two absolutely positioned elements use position-anchor:--a and position-area:center center. Their inset values are10px and auto. The two synchronous test callbacks read computed styles and compare every physical inset string; no page mutation follows the assertions.


Evidence: [testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-getComputedStyle-004.html:1-54](978438c9-a9f0-52e9-a694-4b4a144eeb6c.md)

## (anonymous) (unit-2)

Reads computed styles of t2, whose inset is auto, then requires top,left,bottom,right all to resolve to0px when position-area is non-initial. The callback returns undefined after four assertions.


Evidence: [testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-getComputedStyle-004.html:47-53](ec511f62-fb4d-5368-a3a5-af7f607436e9.md)

## (anonymous) (unit-3)

Reads computed styles of t1, whose inset is10px, then requires top,left,bottom,right all to remain10px despite position-area. The callback returns undefined after four assertions.


